/Pg 22 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
308 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 125 0 R
/E (Refugees and asylum seekers experience complex health challenges due to difficult conditions before, during, and after seeking safety. These challenges include both physical and mental health issues. They are often linked to trauma, limited healthcare access, and resettlement difficulties.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
309 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 125 0 R
/E (Physical health challenges may include untreated chronic illnesses \(such as diabetes and hypertension\), infectious diseases, poor nutrition, and fatigue. )
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
310 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 125 0 R
/E (Mental health challenges are also common, including trauma, post-traumatic stress disorder \(PTSD\), anxiety, depression, grief, and social isolation. These issues are frequently linked to experiences of war, displacement, loss, and ongoing stress in a new environment. )
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
311 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 125 0 R
/E (Overall, these health challenges are often interconnected and may be worsened by social factors such as loneliness, financial hardship, and barriers to healthcare access. )
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
